ped away evidence of espionage or even reconnaissance for future sabotage.<=
/p></div></blockquote></aside></div><p class=3D"paywall">All told, Snabe es=
timated in his Davos comments, NotPetya cost Maersk between $250 million an=
d $300 million. Most of the staffers WIRED spoke with privately suspected t=
he company=E2=80=99s accountants had low-balled the figure.</p><p class=3D"=
paywall">Regardless, those numbers only start to describe the magnitude of =
the damage. Logistics companies whose livelihoods depend on Maersk-owned te=
rminals weren=E2=80=99t all treated as well during the outage as Maersk=E2=
=80=99s customers, for instance. Jeffrey Bader, president of a Port Newark=
=E2=80=93based trucking group, the Association of Bi-State Motor Carriers, =
estimates that the unreimbursed cost for trucking companies and truckers al=
one is in the tens of millions. =E2=80=9CIt was a nightmare,=E2=80=9D Bader=
 says. =E2=80=9CWe lost a lot of money, and we=E2=80=99re angry.=E2=80=9D</=
p><p class=3D"paywall">The wider cost of Maersk=E2=80=99s disruption to the=
 global supply chain as a whole=E2=80=94which depends on just-in-time deliv=
ery of products and manufacturing components=E2=80=94is far harder to measu=
re. And, of course, Maersk was only one victim. Merck, whose ability to man=
ufacture some drugs was temporarily shut down by NotPetya, told shareholder=
s it lost a staggering $870 million due to the malware. FedEx, whose Europe=
an subsidiary TNT Express was crippled in the attack and required months to=
 recover some data, took a $400 million blow. French construction giant Sai=
nt-Gobain lost around the same amount. Reckitt Benckiser, the British manuf=
acturer of Durex condoms, lost $129 million, and Mondel=C4=93z, the owner o=
f chocolate-maker Cadbury, took a $188 million hit. Untold numbers of victi=
ms without public shareholders counted their losses in secret.</p><p class=
=3D"paywall">Only when you start to multiply Maersk=E2=80=99s story=E2=80=
=94imagining the same paralysis, the same serial crises, the same grueling =
recovery=E2=80=94playing out across dozens of other NotPetya victims and co=
untless other industries does the true scale of Russia=E2=80=99s cyberwar c=
rime begin to come into focus.</p></div></div></div><div class=3D"GridItem-=
